    "biography": {
      "concept": "Cook at the drum-stove cookline at the mouth of Khezek Tor (Act 1-3)",
      "notes": "Bez runs the cookline at the mouth of Khezek Tor: a welded row of drum-stoves, tin plates, granite arms. No requests are taken and none are ever needed. Bez serves and does not narrate; a place gets made for you on the bench by somebody shoving down, not by Bez saying so. The portions are a threat and a promise. Ask for a substitution and you get the same plate, slower. Shift changes, plates come, somebody plays the fiddle badly and is loved for it."
    }
